SUMMARY:Virtual REGISTER: Phil Collins - The Solo Years Musical History
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**Important: When you sign-up\, you will a
 lso need to Register as soon as possible** **to obtain your link to the ev
 ent.**\n\nOn **Saturday October 17th**\, enjoy the music of **Phil Collins
  - The Solo Years**\, **focusing on his career as a solo artist (as oppose
 d to his time with Genesis) during the 1980’s and 1990’s.** During and
  after our program you’ll have the opportunity to participate in an onli
 ne discussion with your fellow music lovers via Zoom. **Register for your 
 virtual link of Phil Collins - the Solo Years. on Saturday October 17h at 
 3pm.**\n\n**Philip David Charles Collins** (born 30 January 1951) is an En
 glish singer\, drummer\, songwriter\, record producer\, and actor. He was 
 the drummer and later became the lead singer of the rock band Genesis and 
 had a successful solo career\, achieving three UK number-one singles and s
 even US number-one singles as a solo artist. In total\, his work with Gene
 sis\, other artists and solo resulted in more US top-40 singles than any o
 ther artist throughout the 1980s. His most successful singles from the per
 iod include "In the Air Tonight"\, "You Can't Hurry Love"\, "Against All O
 dds (Take a Look at Me Now)"\, "One More Night"\, "Sussudio"\, "Another Da
 y in Paradise"\, "Two Hearts" and "I Wish It Would Rain Down".\n\nCollins'
 s discography includes eight studio albums that have sold 33.5 million cer
 tified units in the US and an estimated 150 million records sold worldwide
  as a solo artist\, making him one of the world's best-selling music artis
 ts. He is one of only three recording artists\, along with Paul McCartney 
 and Michael Jackson\, who have sold over 100 million records both as solo 
 artists and separately as principal members of a band. He has won 8 Grammy
  Awards\, six Brit Awards (winning Best British Male Artist three times)\,
  two Golden Globe Awards\, one Academy Award and a Disney Legend Award. He
  was awarded 6 Ivor Novello Awards from the British Academy of Songwriters
 \, Composers and Authors\, including the International Achievement Award. 
 He received a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame in 1999\, was inducted in
 to the Songwriters Hall of Fame in 2003\, the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame a
 s a member of Genesis in 2010\, and as a solo artist in 2026.\n\n**COST**:
  By Donation\, or Free if you're unable to donate. I encourage you to plea
 se donate to the host.\n\n**SIGNING UP**:\n\n* **Simply RSVP Yes and [Regi
 ster](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/phil-collins-the-solo-years-music-histo
 ry-livestream-tickets-1992889852195?aff=ebdsoporgprofile) here to receive 
 your link to the event.**\n* The registration company will send you a conf
 irmation email and two reminder emails with the link prior to start\n* **S
 tart time: at 3pm**\, click on the link provided to join the event\n* Leng
 th: estimate 2 hours\n*\n\nEnjoy and please post your Comments in the even
 t after.\n\nI encourage you to donate to the host via:\n**PayPal**: DCHist
 oryAndCulture@gmail.com\n**Venmo**: @DCHistoryAndCulture\n**GoFundMe**: ht
 tps://gofund.me/d29491c0\n\nIf you have questions/ need help\, please cont
 act rkelleman@yahoo.com or https://www.eventbrite.com/support/articles/en_
 US/Troubleshooting/did-my-email-send-invitations-order-confirmations-remin
 ders?lg=en_US\n\nRSVPs close 2 days prior hoping there will still be free 
 spots\; cancellations may result in a No Show.
